  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your disguise incorporates hidden magic items that you can activate while pretending to use your own magic. As part of creating the disguise, you can hide up to 2 carried magic items on your person, attempting a Sleight of Hand check for each one as normal (note many items, such as wands, are small enough to grant a bonus on this check). You can use your Disguise modifier for these Sleight of Hand checks if it is better.</p>\n<p>For every 5 ranks in the associated skill you possess, you can incorporate an additional magic item into the disguise. You can activate items incorporated into your spellcaster disguise as if you were holding them in hand and observers cannot tell you did not cast the magic yourself unless they succeed at an opposed Perception or Spellcraft check (using whichever modifier is higher) against your Sleight of Hand result to hide it on your person.</p>\n<p>Whenever you successfully activate a magic item that is not incorporated into the disguise, you can attempt a Sleight of Hand check to pretend you cast the spell without the item’s help. Again, observers believe the ruse unless they succeed at an opposed Perception or Spellcraft check (using whichever modifier is higher).</p>\n<hr>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/subterfuge#toc36\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
